WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:07.140
Fundraising software that doesn't live in your Salesforce org.

2
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.525
Lives somewhere else.

3
00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.433
Your donation platform holds the donors.

4
00:00:12.433 --> 00:00:14.812
Salesforce gets a copy overnight.

5
00:00:14.812 --> 00:00:16.975
And the two never quite agree.

6
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.877
Pledgivo removes the second system.

7
00:00:20.877 --> 00:00:21.523
One org.

8
00:00:21.523 --> 00:00:23.300
One copy of the truth.

9
00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:27.241
A public donation form, backed by Stripe.

10
00:00:27.241 --> 00:00:32.592
The card is tokenized in the browser, and the gift lands as an Opportunity.

11
00:00:33.583 --> 00:00:38.147
Salesforce owns the schedule and charges the saved card itself.

12
00:00:38.147 --> 00:00:42.058
No subscription living in another system to reconcile.

13
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:50.200
Every appeal is a standard Salesforce Campaign, with a page design that themes the whole donor experience.

14
00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:58.083
Ticketed events with tiered pricing and real seat capacity, on the same pipeline as every other gift.

15
00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:01.426
Donors update their own giving.

16
00:01:01.426 --> 00:01:03.089
A code in their inbox.

17
00:01:03.089 --> 00:01:05.583
No account, no password to reset.

18
00:01:06.783 --> 00:01:08.006
And it travels.

19
00:01:08.006 --> 00:01:12.733
Two lines of HTML put a live campaign on any site you own.

20
00:01:14.083 --> 00:01:16.901
A managed package on the current API.

21
00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:19.566
Payment keys in a Named Credential.

22
00:01:19.566 --> 00:01:22.383
No public webhook endpoint to secure.

23
00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:24.006
Pledgivo.

24
00:01:24.006 --> 00:01:27.258
Keep your donors where your data already lives.

